  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate ${T}^{\u2032}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t+1)\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t+1)\\,k)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t+1))\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t+1))\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t+1)\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t+1)\\,k)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{\u2032}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\frac{1}{2}\u2016\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t+1)\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t+1)\\,k\u2016 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t+1))^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t+1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}\u2061(t+1)+{sin}^{2}\u2061(t+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{\u2032}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{\u2032}(t)}{\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t+1)\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t+1)\\,k)}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t+1)\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t+1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$",
